{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf959J51W4WLg2oxmEXP6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WLPqoFgp7FdqrNyfoidqdb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"Implement BE-005: partial fulfilment, customer validation, and pagination\n\n- Orders and shipments gain quantity field with validation for positive integers\n- Shipments allocate against order quantity, preventing over-allocation\n- Orders track fulfilment status (UNALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED)\n- Orders can be filtered by fulfilment status with GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS\n- Order quantities can be amended with PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity\n- Shipment transitions: POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm, deliver, cancel\n- Cancelling shipment releases its quantity for re-allocation\n- Customer validation: orders can only be created for existing customers (HTTP 422)\n- GET /customers/{customerId} returns 404 through error envelope\n- Pagination: GET /customers, /orders, /shipments accept limit (1-100, default 100) and offset (0+, default 0)\n- X-Total-Count header included in paginated responses\n- OrderControllerTest updated to create customers before creating orders\n- All existing tests pass\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" -- sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerRepository.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt sample-service/src/m