a0aeeb54c && git add -A && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nImplement partial fulfilment, customer validation, and pagination\n\n1. Partial fulfilment: Orders and shipments now have quantity field. Shipments\n   allocate against order quantity, with validation to prevent over-allocation.\n   Orders track fulfilment status (UNALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, FULLY_ALLOCATED,\n   DELIVERED) and can be filtered by this status. Order quantities can be amended\n   after shipments exist.\n\n2. Customer validation: Orders can only be created for existing customers. Attempting\n   to create an order for a non-existent customer returns HTTP 422. GET /customers\n   for unknown customer returns HTTP 404 through the error envelope.\n\n3. Pagination: GET endpoints for customers, orders, and shipments accept limit\n   (1-100, default 100) and offset (0+, default 0) parameters. Responses include\n   X-Total-Count header with total item count before slicing.\n\n4. Shipment transitions: Added confirm, deliver, and cancel endpoints to transition\n   shipments through their lifecycle (CREATED -> CONFIRMED -> DELIVERED, or\n   CREATED -> CANCELLED). Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.\n\nAll existing tests pass. OrderControllerTest updated to create customers before\ncreating orders.\nEOF\n)\""}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GyNH9WdJUZrxUvoSggUKKP","tool_input":{"command":"git add -A && git log --oneline -5"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQZNqKe1QjNQVgL9bXtfh2","tool_input":{"command":"git add sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerRepository.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt sam